//
// PHI-4-MINI Q4NX prefill TTFT vs prompt length, into
// phi4_mini_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark).
// The other axis from run_npu2_sweep.lit: that one walks KV depth for decode
// tok/s, this one walks how many tokens the prefill computes. They cannot
// share a table -- one is throughput against cache depth, the other is latency
// against problem size.
//
// It times the fused prefill, the one run, verify and profile use. That prefill
// is chunked and takes any prompt up to the length it was built for, so
// sweep_prefill.py --fused builds it once, for the longest length, and times
// every length in one process on a synthetic prompt of exactly that length.
//
// Unlike the decode sweep this needs real weights -- a prefill is a prefill.
// It needs only the q4nx bundle, though, NOT the base HF checkpoint that
// run_npu2_profile.lit also requires: the fused prefill loads its weights from
// the bundle alone and the bench prompts with synthetic token ids, so it builds
// no tokenizer.
// Requiring the base checkpoint anyway would silently SKIP the point on a
// runner that lacks it, and drop the model's row from the published table.
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate (run_npu2_verify.lit is that).
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, llvm_link_pre23, hf_token, hfweights_fastflowlm_phi4_mini_instruct_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name phi4_mini_q4nx --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,2048,8192,32768 --fused --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out phi4_mini_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < phi4_mini_q4nx.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "phi4_mini_q4nx"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// A parsed number at the reference length, not just a well-formed file: if the
// bench's timing line drifts out of sweep_prefill.py's regex every point goes
// null and the published curve silently empties while the test stays green.
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
